Our Global Structure
Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we're unlocking new possibilities as one global team.Join us in our mission to transform the way people shop and eat, where impact, innovation, and growth drives everything we do. Our Finance team shapes the company's future by directing capital to high-impact investments, developing robust financial strategies, and ensuring we deliver long-term value while pursuing our ambitious mission.
&nbsp;
We're looking for a Senior Manager, Corporate Services Sourcing to join our team. This is a remote role based in Europe (preferred hubs: London, Berlin, Copenhagen, or Helsinki). In this role, you'll help us lead the Corporate Services Sourcing team for the Deliveroo and Wolt brands, driving strategic category management and delivering commercial value across a multi-million-pound indirect spend portfolio.
&nbsp;
Get to know our Finance team — what drives us, how we work, and what you can expect.
&nbsp;
What You'll Be Doing
You'll be joining the Global Sourcing team within our Global Procurement organization, reporting into the Director, Head of Global Strategic Sourcing. You will lead a team of five (5) managing a broad portfolio across EMEA (including Professional Services, Global Security, Facilities/Real Estate, BPO, HR/Benefits, and Contingent Workforce), while partnering with the DoorDash Corporate Services team to capture global enterprise synergies.
&nbsp;
Here's what your day-to-day might look like:
&nbsp;
Category Strategy &amp; Leadership


Lead and develop a high-performing sourcing team of five, setting clear goals, driving accountability, and building capability across the Corporate Services portfolio.
&nbsp;


Build and execute multi-year category strategies that increase category maturity, optimise total cost of ownership (TCO), and unlock value beyond traditional cost savings.
&nbsp;


Partner with DoorDash sourcing leads to align global category strategies, leverage enterprise scale across brands, and capture cross-regional synergies.
&nbsp;


Execution &amp; Supplier Management


Own the end-to-end sourcing lifecycle for high-stakes corporate procurement, including data analysis, RFx creation, proposal evaluation, and complex contract negotiations (MSAs/SOWs).
&nbsp;


Act as a trusted advisor and escalation point for executive stakeholders across G&amp;A functions (Finance, Legal, HR, Security) and core business lines.
&nbsp;


Establish best-in-class supplier ecosystems, tracking performance, SLAs, and supplier risk while embedding ethical and sustainable sourcing (ESG) practices.
&nbsp;


Contribute to procurement transformation initiatives, championing new tooling, AI-driven sourcing workflows, and continuous process improvements.
&nbsp;


What You'll Need to Thrive
Essential


Significant experience in Corporate Services Sourcing, with a proven track record of developing and executing strategic category plans across indirect spend categories.
&nbsp;


Demonstrated people management capability, with experience leading, mentoring, and developing high-performing sourcing professionals.
&nbsp;


Strong commercial and negotiation acumen, with proven ability to structure and negotiate complex commercial agreements (MSAs, SOWs) and utilise TCO modelling.
&nbsp;


Exceptional stakeholder engagement and communication skills, capable of influencing senior leaders, managing matrixed business partners, and driving cross-brand collaboration.
&nbsp;


Deep risk management expertise, including third-party risk assessments, contract governance, and mitigation strategies within multi-jurisdictional environments.
&nbsp;


Nice to Have


Experience working within the technology sector or high-growth, fast-paced marketplace environments.
&nbsp;


Proficiency with modern procurement and CLM platforms (e.g., Coupa, NetSuite, Pivot) and enthusiasm for applying AI tools in day-to-day sourcing workflows.
&nbsp;


Experience operating across European markets and diverse regulatory/legal structures.
&nbsp;


Why Join Us?
At Deliveroo, you'll do work that matters, solving real-world problems in a three-sided marketplace that's constantly evolving.
We're food lovers, problem solvers, community builders and more, brought together by a shared drive to make things better. Working here you can expect to:
&nbsp;
🔧 Make a visible impact every day
Your work directly improves experiences for customers, partners and riders.
&nbsp;
🌱 Learn fast in an entrepreneurial environment
Work close to the market with autonomy, pace and real responsibility.
&nbsp;
🧠 Build a career, not just a role
Stretch yourself, develop new skills and grow as the business evolves.
&nbsp;
🌎 Deliver together in an inclusive culture
Collaborative, values-driven teams that support how you work best.
&nbsp;
We aim to create a fair process that lets your skills shine—our interview typically includes 3-4 stages. Find more about how we hire here.
&nbsp;Diversity, Equity and InclusionAt Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We're committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.
We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.
If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you'll have the opportunity to let us know once you've submitted your application. We'll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.
If you're excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we'd love to hear from you!
Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands' legitimate recruiting process at careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness.Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Operational Excellence Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be the architect of efficiency for our Australia and New Zealand markets. Sitting at the intersection of Planning, FSQA, Procurement, and Fulfillment, you will define our Target Operating Model (TOM) and drive the strategic framework that ensures our end-to-end (E2E) supply chain is lean, scalable, and resilient.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in &lt;strong&gt;Chippendale, Sydney&lt;/strong&gt; and reports to the &lt;strong&gt;Associate Director of Operations Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the ANZ Operational Excellence strategy, translating business goals into a multi-year roadmap tailored to local market nuances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain the Target Operating Model (TOM) to ensure clear accountability, escalation governance, and seamless hand-offs across Planning, Procurement, FSQA, and Fulfillment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a portfolio of high-complexity projects using Lean, Six Sigma, or Kaizen methodologies to drive step-change improvements in Cost per Box (CPB), Cost of Goods Sold (COGS), and operational error rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify E2E supply chain bottlenecks and standardize tools and systems to reduce manual intervention, enhance data integrity, and drive supply chain digitalization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a robust project governance framework and analyze cross-functional performance data to prioritize high-leverage opportunities for waste reduction and cost optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a Continuous Improvement (CI) DNA across ANZ by designing training programs, coaching regional teams, and scaling best practices across our network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary bridge for ANZ leadership to ensure operational consistency and alignment across all business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep operational expertise across Supply Chain pillars (Planning, FSQA, Procurement, and Fulfillment) within high-growth, complex environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing Target Operating Models and E2E frameworks, along with a track record of leading large-scale organizational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated mastery in project governance and continuous improvement methodologies (such as Lean, Six Sigma, or Kaizen) with a history of delivering measurable ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and technical judgement, with the ability to use data-driven insights to identify systemic issues and drive financial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic, systems-level thinker who anticipates E2E supply chain impacts and moves proactively from reactive troubleshooting to systemic prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An influential communicator with high emotional intelligence, capable of pitching process improvements to the C-suite and running Kaizen events on the warehouse floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous and results-oriented, bringing a &quot;Founder’s Mentality&quot; to navigate ambiguity and take full accountability for cross-functional KPIs without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural coach and mentor who leads by example, challenges the status quo, and elevates the problem-solving capabilities of peers and operational leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get in return…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to have a significant impact in a leading global food technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working arrangements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Egoless environment, constant learning with room for personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free access to Headspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal learning &amp;amp; development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A diverse and vibrant international environment, with offices in 18 countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company discount - 70% off HelloFresh &amp;amp; 40% off Youfoodz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start Date: &lt;/strong&gt;Immediately available - Can wait a notice period&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration: &lt;/strong&gt;Permanent full time role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Chippendale Head Office - hybrid working environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary: &lt;/strong&gt;Competitive salary &amp;amp; employee benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#S-DNI #LI-DNI&lt;/p&gt;
