Job Description
Ben jij klaar om jouw carrière naar grote hoogte te tillen? Stap in als Liftmonteur! Van woontorens tot grote infraprojecten: jij werkt op unieke locaties door heel Nederland en zorgt ervoor dat onze bouwliften veilig en betrouwbaar functioneren.

Jouw baan als Liftmonteur bij RECO
Als Liftmonteur in de buitendienst bij RECO werk je op de meest uiteenlopende bouwprojecten door heel Nederland. Samen met ervaren collega's monteer en demonteer je tijdelijke personen- en goederenliften, voer je onderhoud uit en zorg je ervoor dat onze liften veilig en betrouwbaar functioneren. Je werkt veel in de buitenlucht, op grote hoogte en op locaties waar geen dag hetzelfde is. Terwijl Nederland nog wakker moet worden, geniet jij al van de mooiste uitzichten.
Jouw belangrijkste werkzaamheden:
✅ Monteren en demonteren van tijdelijke personen- en goederenliften aan de hand van technische tekeningen.
✅ Laden en lossen van liftonderdelen en materialen met de vrachtwagen.
✅ Uitvoeren van onderhoud, inspecties en kleine reparaties aan liften.
✅ Ondersteunen bij het oplossen van technische storingen op locatie.
✅ Schakelen met klanten, uitvoerders, steigerbouwers en collega's om ieder project veilig en efficiënt uit te voeren.
Requirements

Wat breng jij mee?
👍 Je bent 40 uur per week beschikbaar van 6-15 uur;👍 Je hebt geen hoogtevrees;👍 Je hebt een goede beheersing van de Nederlandse taal;👍 Je hebt technisch inzicht en werkervaring op het gebied van mechatronisch en bij voorkeur ook elektrotechniek;👍 Je hebt een rijbewijs B in bezit;👍 Je bent in het bezit van je VCA-certificaat óf wil deze via ons behalen;👍 Je bent een echte doener, neemt initiatief en kunt goed samenwerken.
Bij RECO willen we jou blij maken met:
✅ Een goed salaris;
✅ 28 vakantiedagen per jaar, oplopend tot 31 dagen als waardering voor geen ziekteverzuim;
✅ Overwerkvergoeding;
✅ Buitendienstvergoeding;
✅ Een collectieve zorgverzekering én goede pensioenregeling met maar 3,3% eigen bijdrage, de rest betaalt RECO;
✅ Een moderne werkbus gevuld met het nieuwste gereedschap;
✅ Een mobiele telefoon van de zaak;
✅ Veel opleidings- en ontwikkelmogelijkheden via onze RECO Academy;
✅ Werken in een hechte organisatie: iedereen kent elkaar bij naam, de lijnen zijn kort en je loopt gemakkelijk bij elkaar binnen. Daarnaast organiseren we een goed verzorgde zomerbarbecue en een groots eindejaarspersoneelsfeest! Klik hier voor een kijkje in onze .
Over RECO
RECOis dé specialist in het verhuren van bouwplaats materialen voor uiteenlopende projecten in de bouw, infra, renovatie, overheid en evenementen. Met een aanpakkers mentaliteit en betrokken collega’s werken we samen aan slimme materieeloplossingen.Find more English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The role:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Token Factory analytics there is no split into product analysts, ML engineers and data engineers. Each person owns a question end to end: builds the data, runs the analysis, and comes back with a recommendation that changes a decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Define core product and business metrics and build a single source of truth that Product, Finance, and Sales can rely on.&lt;br&gt;- Build a comprehensive view of self-service customers, including usage patterns, customer health, satisfaction, retention risks, unmet needs, and growth opportunities.&lt;br&gt;- Translate customer demand and commercial plans into capacity forecasts and support capacity allocation decisions.&lt;br&gt;- Measure effective capacity utilization and identify opportunities to improve the commercial value of available capacity.&lt;br&gt;- Develop and evaluate pricing and packaging models, including guaranteed capacity, on-demand pricing, commitments, clawback mechanisms, and provisioned throughput units.&lt;br&gt;- Provide data-driven recommendations for the self-service and managed offerings, including customer segmentation, pricing, and capacity.&lt;br&gt;- Partner with Product, Engineering, Applied AI, Finance, and Sales to turn insights into concrete product and operational improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 5+ years of experience in analytics or data science.&lt;br&gt;- Strong Python, SQL, and statistics: you understand the code and the methods you use.&lt;br&gt;- Hands-on experience analysing large-scale customer, product, and usage datasets using statistical / analytical or distributed data-processing tools.&lt;br&gt;- AI-assisted coding as your default way of working: you guide it, verify it, and own the result.&lt;br&gt;- The ability to go from a question to a production-ready solution.&lt;br&gt;- The ability to turn complex data into clear recommendations.&lt;br&gt;- Strong commercial and product judgment, with the ability to balance customer value, monetization, growth, and profitability.&lt;br&gt;- Experience with pricing, packaging, monetization, or commercial analytics for technical or consumption-based products.&lt;br&gt;- Strong cross-functional collaboration skills across Product, Engineering, Data, Finance, Sales, and Operations.&lt;br&gt;- A hands-on and proactive working style, with the ability to operate effectively in an ambiguous and technically complex environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Familiarity with LLM inference economics: tokens, throughput and latency, batching, GPU costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Real Chemistry, making the world a healthier place isn’t just an aspiration—it’s our everyday reality. Our drive to transform healthcare is informed by our blend of deep scientific expertise, human-centred creativity, and AI-driven insights, fostering a unique environment where innovation thrives and our people are impact-obsessed. As a global agency, we provide a full suite of services across healthcare communications and marketing to our clients, including top players in the pharmaceutical and biotech industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our #LifeatRealChem culture is rooted in our people—we believe we are best together and are committed to excellence for both our clients and colleagues. Whether you&#39;re a seasoned professional or just starting your career, if you share our passion for healthcare and connection, we invite you to explore our opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Discover your purpose. Embrace innovation. Experience #LifeatRealChem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real Chemistry is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Account Director&lt;/strong&gt; to join our growing team!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Account Director&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be responsible for excellence in delivery across projects within medium-to-large and often complex client accounts. You will provide strategic counsel to clients, manage execution of parallel ongoing projects and oversee a cross-functional internal team alongside the account lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be supporting on some of our promotional medical education accounts and include projects such as events and patient-based campaigns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the go-to for clients, managing relationships and setting their expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take accountability for a portfolio of projects within at least two medium-to-large client accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure work is delivered to the highest standard and within agreed timeframes and budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and provide solutions to client challenges and last-minute requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify areas for organic growth within existing accounts and confidently sell new ideas to clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new business opportunities outside of existing accounts and explore with the support of senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the ongoing new business process, assisting in the production of credentials and participating in broader RFP responses when possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and empower your team on a daily basis, leading by example and setting the standard for junior accounts team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide line management, coaching and mentoring to junior team members and manage their performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility for financial management of your client business and participate actively in the monthly financial process (including developing budgets)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately forecast and proactively alert senior leadership to any changes/potential slowing down of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is a perfect fit for you if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Company values –&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Best Together, Impact-Obsessed, Excellence Expected, Evolve Always&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;Accountability with an “I”&lt;/em&gt; – really speak to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are adaptable, resilient, and OK with adjusting your scope, responsibilities, and focus as we grow. When things change, so do we. We’re always evolving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are proactive, driven, and resourceful with strong prioritization skills and a desire to dive into the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are highly organized self-starter, able to work independently and under tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an Associate Account Director, or Senior Account Manager looking to step up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a medical communications agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on promotional medical education or commercial medical affairs accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work within and lead cross-functional teams internally&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with annual planning, resourcing, and forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous line management experience (ideally have had at least one formal linee)&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Real Chemistry is proud to be Great Place to Work®&amp;nbsp;certified; check out what our people shared about our culture and workplace on our Great Places to Work Profile&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.greatplacetowork.com%2Fcertified-company%2F7038366&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cclehmar%40realchemistry.com%7C1f18aaed4326491b3efc08ddd690f025%7C6fa5bfc4f95843f8bb395d382689654b%7C0%7C0%7C638902640185888156%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=pwvaCn37QXkjVQ0p6u92Oz4FA4j5NQZoNJL0ffy01qs%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe we can do our best when feeling our best, which is why we’ve put together a benefits program designed to give you the support you and your family need at every stage of life. Real Chemistry offers a comprehensive benefit program and perks, tailored to your region. Globally, this includes offices in our key markets with free snacks to keep you running all day long, generous holiday and paid time off, options for private medical, dental, and vison plans, and support in saving for the future. Other perks include mental wellness coaching and support&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;access to more than 13,000 online classes with LinkedIn Learning.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Learn more about our great benefits and perks and search specific offerings in your region at:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.realchemistrybenefits.com&quot;&gt;www.realchemistrybenefits.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;At Real Chemistry, we believe we&#39;re at our best when we&#39;re connected. Our Real Hybrid and Regional Teams (Real HART) approach is designed to foster collaboration, learning, innovation, and meaningful relationships while providing flexibility where appropriate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Because our workforce spans multiple countries, regions, and client needs, work arrangements may vary by role and location. Some positions offer hybrid or remote flexibility, while others require regular in-office presence. For example, certain teams and regions, including some of our UK operations, have office-based requirements. Your recruiter will discuss the specific expectations for the role you&#39;re pursuing during the interview process and keep you informed throughout the hiring journey.&amp;nbsp;For employees located within a one-hour commute of a Real Chemistry office, we require in-person attendance two days per week, either from a Real Chemistry office or when working onsite with clients. Employees in regions without a nearby office may work remotely and come together throughout the year for collaboration, culture-building, learning, and team connection opportunities.&amp;nbsp;While these guidelines reflect our current workplace model, we understand that everyone’s circumstances are unique. If you require additional flexibility, we welcome an open conversation with your recruiter and our HR team to discuss your needs and determine what may be possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real Chemistry is an Equal Opportunity employer. We continually strive to build and sustain an inclusive and equitable work environment where our employees feel empowered to leverage all they bring from their personal lived experience and professional expertise, to make our team the best in the industry. We encourage motivated and qualified applicants to apply without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, ethnic or national origin, age, physical or mental disability, genetic information, marital information, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local employment discrimination laws where Real Chemistry operates. Should you require accommodations throughout the interview process please let your recruiter know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Notice: Real Chemistry and its affiliates&#39; names are being misused by scammers through messaging services, fake websites, and apps. Do not share personal or financial information or make payments to any unverified sources claiming to be connected to Real Chemistry. We are working to stop these unauthorized activities and protect our community. Read more&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.realchemistry.com%2Fscam-alert&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cclehmar%40realchemistry.com%7C1f18aaed4326491b3efc08ddd690f025%7C6fa5bfc4f95843f8bb395d382689654b%7C0%7C0%7C638902640185967986%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=vBa1KYjD6TUHgTF3FdPRQZvM8E8WUgHZqu9yHevh1%2BI%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Product Manager to join our Agentic Search team, building the search and retrieval infrastructure that powers AI agents and LLM-based applications at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on IC role with real ownership. You will take full end-to-end responsibility over a core product area, from defining strategy through shipping and iterating based on real usage data. You will work within a small PM team reporting to the Director of Product, alongside engineering, design, and go-to-market, shaping how AI agents discover, retrieve, and act on web information in real time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The product serves both a developer-facing PLG motion and a growing enterprise customer base, so you will need to be equally comfortable digging into API design and search quality as you are running customer discovery calls and informing competitive positioning. We are looking for someone who can operate as a senior strategic partner, not just an executor, and who has the potential to grow into a principal-level PM over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re welcome to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;work hybrid from Tel Aviv, Israel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360}&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW95146830 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW95146830 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW95146830 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a core product area end-to-end: strategy, roadmap, execution, and iteration based on real usage signals and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive search quality and relevance improvements by working closely with engineering and research to define evaluation frameworks, benchmarks, and release criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with enterprise customers and developer users to validate ideas, understand pain points, and shape product-market fit across both PLG and enterprise motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the competitive landscape in agentic search and AI-powered retrieval, identifying shifts, threats, and opportunities that should inform product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with go-to-market teams (sales, solutions, growth) to ensure product positioning, ICP definitions, and enablement materials reflect product reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to product strategy as a senior voice on a small, high-impact team, challenging assumptions and bringing independent judgment to key decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product experiments and rapid iteration cycles, moving from hypothesis to prototype to production with clear success criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, with a meaningful portion in developer tools, API platforms, or search and retrieval infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of shipping products in fast-moving markets, working closely with engineering and design from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of LLMs, AI agents, and how search and retrieval systems fit into agentic workflows. Hands-on technical background is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in computer science, engineering, or a related field, with the ability to engage deeply with technical architecture and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguity: you can context-switch between strategic thinking and tactical execution without losing the thread.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and drive alignment without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication: you can explain technical concepts clearly to both engineers and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;It will be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;an added bonus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt; if you have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in search, information retrieval, NLP, or adjacent domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in API-first or developer-platform businesses with both PLG and enterprise motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience in a high-growth technology company, especially post-acquisition or startup-within-a-larger-org environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People management or mentoring experience (building the skills of other PMs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

Senior Fire, Health &amp; Safety Consultant | Hybrid | London &amp; Surrounding | Permanent | Competitive Package
&nbsp;
At Ark Workplace Risk, we empower our clients to confidently manage risk, compliance, and safety through a trusted partnership built on expert knowledge, innovative solutions, and proactive guidance and insight. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
About Ark Workplace Risk:&nbsp;&nbsp;

Proven Expert Knowledge: With over 30 years of experience and a trusted reputation among 200+ UK organisations, we provide workable solutions that align with our clients' organisational and business goals, as well as regulatory requirements. &nbsp;
Industry-Leading Software: Our innovative tools streamline risk and compliance management, putting clients in control and enabling them to demonstrate accountability to stakeholders.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Insight-Driven Solutions: As industry thought leaders, we provide actionable insights into emerging legislation, guidance, and industry trends, ensuring court-readiness for their business.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Responsive Partnership: From every day, business-as-usual guidance to urgent, critical, complex, and contentious scenarios, we work in partnership with clients, becoming their trusted advisor and solution provider, whenever and wherever they need us most.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
About the Role&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Reporting into a Team Leader (each team is circa 5-7) and up to the Director of Professional Services, you will be joining a market leading team of professionals to undertake risk assessments and advise on fire, health and safety matters at&nbsp;a variety of buildings including&nbsp;mid-high rise&nbsp;buildings, to our established portfolio of clients across a variety of segments, including, residential, commercial and retail.&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Responsibilities:&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;Undertake risk assessments including&nbsp;fire and health&nbsp;and safety, ensuring the fee earning target is met.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Undertake various fire,&nbsp;health&nbsp;and safety assignments within your competency.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Deliver client reports within the agreed SLA,&nbsp;in accordance with&nbsp;a forensic and pragmatic approach to ensure the Ark 'Gold Standard' is achieved.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
Design health and safety site management systems where&nbsp;required, specific to client requirements.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Undertake onsite briefings and advise on risk management improvements.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Work collaboratively with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Work with other consultants to ensure we are constantly sharing knowledge across the team.&nbsp;&nbsp;
Demonstrate a comprehensive understanding of controlling risks, compliances etc in relation to our online management system QUOODA®&nbsp;&nbsp;
Remain&nbsp;up-to-date&nbsp;with the Technical and regulatory requirements&nbsp;impacting&nbsp;our clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;&nbsp;
The ideal candidate will have:&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;At least 5+ years'&nbsp;fire, health &amp; safety&nbsp;risk assessment experience within the built environment in residential and/or commercial buildings&nbsp;
Good working knowledge of Approved Document B&nbsp;
Good working knowledge of BS 9999 / 9997&nbsp;
Education suitable to be competent to carry out Fire and Health &amp; Safety risk assessments on seven or more floors&nbsp;
The ability to&nbsp;undertake Fire Risk Assessments and General Risk Assessments at the same time&nbsp;
Articulate and clear communicators and report writing abilities as well as a comprehensive understanding of current UK regulations&nbsp;

&nbsp;
&nbsp;Qualifications&nbsp;

Must have NEBOSH General Certificate in Health &amp; Safety or equivalent as minimum.&nbsp;
Recognised fire safety memberships e.g.&nbsp;AIFireE, MIFireE,&nbsp;GIFireE, MIFSM or MIFPO (ADVANTAGEOUS)&nbsp;
Willing to apply for or have registered on any of the following fire risk&nbsp;assessors&nbsp;registers IFSM, FRACS, IFPO or IFE&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Why Work for Us&nbsp;&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Ark is a market leader providing an innovative suite of; Professional Service Solutions, Outsourcing and future-proofed Software and Analytics to mid/major organisations in the UK. With over 500 global and premium brands trusting Ark to deliver smarter Risk, Compliance, Safety.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Reasons to join for us:

An attractive package and training bursary contract.
New game changing Building Safety software.&nbsp;
Options to mentor others and management progression within Ark.&nbsp;
Progress your career with continuous training and CPD opportunities.&nbsp;
Ark is an innovative growing company that is recognised as a leader in safety within the built environment.&nbsp;
Ark organises technical and knowledge sharing which is of enormous benefit to the Ark Professional Services Team.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
APPLY NOW&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Don't&nbsp;believe you have the skills or attributes listed?&nbsp;
