&lt;div class=&quot;overview-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re always hiring software engineers for all of our offices. Technology is at the core of how we approach our work, and engineers are intimately involved in every area of the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are big believers in functional programming and use OCaml, a statically typed functional programming language, as our primary tool. More recently, Python has become a vital part of Jane Street’s research and trading work, acting as the go-to language for data analysis, visualization, and machine learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also believe in the value of open source software, using it in our daily work and releasing over a million lines of our own code as open source.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top-notch programming skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with—and love for—technology. There&#39;s no specific checklist; we use software to approach a variety of problems, so we&#39;re interested in everything from machine learning to systems administration to programming language design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills. Software engineering at Jane Street is highly collaborative, and we are looking for people who can work effectively in small, close-knit teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We &lt;em&gt;don’t &lt;/em&gt;expect you to have experience with functional programming, OCaml, Python, or finance; we’re happy to hire talented engineers and teach them what they need to know.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;d like to get an idea of what we cover in our software engineering interview process, you can visit our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.janestreet.com/preparing-for-a-software-engineering-interview/&quot;&gt;interview prep page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Network Engineer who can help us scale our networks to meet increasing business demands, drive standardisation through automation and look for opportunities to leverage AI to improve operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jane Street’s numerous distributed systems run on a multi-vendor, highly available network infrastructure and handle a variety of traffic profiles – from high-speed trading to everyday internet connectivity. A typical day on the Network Engineering team includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating on new data centre and colocation initiatives, WAN routing optimisation and other cross-team design projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interfacing with stakeholders to assess business needs and develop innovative network features/capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading both reactive support tasks and proactive infrastructure improvements, focusing on thorough documentation to reduce outages and enhance troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exploring AI/ML-driven enhancements to streamline operations and continuously improve service quality Using your networking expertise to help us scale our team’s infrastructure at large while maintaining high standards for network performance and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documenting solutions and processes that help the team work more efficiently, using a meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a passion for innovating within a complex network ecosystem, enjoy building scalable systems and documentation structures and are curious about how AI can refine network operations, this role provides a platform to make a significant impact at Jane Street. We look forward to learning from your expertise and unique perspective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 7+ years of experience operating and deploying network infrastructure, with 3+ years dedicated to ground-up network design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep experience with routing and network protocols (OSPF, BGP, PIM-SM) and the troubleshooting of transport protocols (TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in Linux environments and proficient in at least one programming language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strongly inclined to automate workflows and explore AI/ML approaches to improve efficiency or reduce overhead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eager to produce comprehensive, scalable documentation that benefits the entire team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a demonstrated ability to balance multiple priorities, switch contexts effectively and maintain a high level of customer service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent collaborator and communicator; ready to build strong partnerships with diverse global teams and stakeholders to share your recommendations, issues and outcomes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a flexible, reliable mindset and enthusiasm for sharing knowledge with peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any prior exposure to overlay networks (EVPN, VXLAN) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Network Engineer to join our Network Security team to help us to run, scale and continuously improve our network security infrastructure through hands-on operations, design, and implementation. The ideal candidate would have strong networking fundamentals and experience with security appliances such as firewalls and proxy to join our Network Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jane Street’s numerous distributed systems are built on an agile, reliable, multi-vendor network infrastructure that supports all traffic profiles, from trading to internet connectivity. Supporting such a large multi-function network requires advanced tooling for monitoring and automation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills will be needed to collaborate with colleagues across the firm globally. You will find and resolve issues, plan and execute deployments, and improve systems where possible. In this role, we’ll look to leverage your advanced networking skills and security knowledge to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Network Engineering on design and deployment of security perimeter and adjacent network infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage and continuously evolve network segmentation, DMZ, and other aspects of network security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and lab test new platforms for our network security infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Cybersecurity on detection and mitigation of threats and vulnerabilities on our network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with application owners and traders to enable business workflows in a secure way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively enhance support by improving network infrastructure observability, scripting, and communicating requirements to our software engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve our network security processes and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A holistic approach to system design is critical for this role. The Networking department prioritizes flexibility, compatibility, and efficiency when crafting solutions, all while seeking ongoing buy-in and feedback from users across the firm. Our firm’s culture prizes intellectual humility, openness, and continuous improvement, which translates directly to the daily work of this team. We’re all partners working towards shared goals and are always looking for the next best idea that will make our work stronger.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your strong communication skills and analytical thinking will be invaluable as we support the daily work of our colleagues and keep our systems operating at the highest standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience operating and deploying network infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with routing and network protocols (OSPF, BGP, PIM-SM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting transport protocols (TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of firewall hardware architecture, performance metrics, and its functional components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with firewall configuration and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Public Key Infrastructure and related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of modern encryption techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High capacity to learn; we are interested in how you think, not just what you know&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to context switch, while still being able to prioritize and organize your stack&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally experience with overlay networks (EVPN, VxLAN)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible and reliable team player who enjoys working in a collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a programming language is preferred but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out -----Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for a Market Data Specialist to join our Metadata team, working on improving and supporting our internal golden copy Security Master and Corporate Action Management systems. You’ll be responsible for configuring our systems to improve data quality, helping with data cleaning and validation, solving support issues for internal clients, and interfacing with our data providers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You’ll be embedded into the Metadata Systems Engineering team and will work with software developers, traders, and operations professionals across the firm.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Responsibilities include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Investigating data quality and reliability issues&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Interfacing with exchanges or data vendors, raising, tracking, and resolving issues&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Helping us (the Metadata team and internal clients) understand our data better&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Potentially advising on solutions, e.g., changing monitoring&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Configuring internal services/tools and adding overrides&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and troubleshooting skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial instrument metadata, especially reference data preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in any language and knowledge of SQL or other database language(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident in a Linux/Unix command-line-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible, organised, and great attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations, support, and customer-centric experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out -----Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;About the Position&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for smart and curious individuals to join our growing team and drive our ML work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.janestreet.com/join-jane-street/machine-learning/&quot;&gt;Machine Learning&lt;/a&gt; team, you&#39;ll build the deep learning models that power our trading strategies, supported by our rapidly growing computing cluster with tens of thousands of high-end GPUs. Trading poses unusual challenges— large models and nonstationary datasets in a competitive multi-agent environment—that force us to search for novel techniques.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Jane Street, our researchers, engineers and traders sit a few feet away from each other and work together to train models, architect systems and run trading strategies. Depending on the day, we might be diving deep into market data, tuning hyperparameters, debugging distributed training performance or studying how our model likes to trade in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll rely on your in-depth knowledge of the machine learning landscape and understanding of a variety of approaches—drawn from LLMs, image models, RL agents, recommendation systems or classical ML methods—to shape the future of ML at Jane Street. You’ll train models for the next generation of our deep learning-based trading strategies, and build the fundamental understanding we need to tackle new markets and situations. You’ll also be hiring new colleagues, attending conferences and teaching techniques to teammates—all of which we consider to be real and impactful parts of the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’ve never thought about a career in finance, you’re in good company. Many of us were in the same position before working here. If you have a curious mind and a passion for solving interesting problems, we have a feeling you’ll fit right in. There’s no fixed set of skills we are looking for, but you should bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience working on empirical ML problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to apply logical and mathematical thinking to all kinds of problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual curiosity and excitement about state-of-the-art research across many ML problem domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with a versatile set of models and tricks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The hands-on coding skills needed to rapidly implement and iterate on your ideas, in Python and your favourite ML framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An eagerness to ask questions, admit mistakes&amp;nbsp; and learn new things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’d like to learn more, you can read about our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.janestreet.com/join-jane-street/ml-research-interviews&quot;&gt;interview process&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.janestreet.com/join-jane-street/get-to-know-us/&quot;&gt;meet some of the team&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you&#39;re a recruiting agency and want to partner with us, please reach out to -----Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div id=&quot;model-response-message-contentr_ce05398d7259c8f0&quot; class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;model-response-message-contentr_ce05398d7259c8f0&quot; class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Notre Team Data lake recherche un·e Senior Product Manager (f/m/d) en CDI basé·e à Lille ou Paris&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Decathlon, nous croyons au pouvoir du sport pour unir et inspirer. Notre mission : au travers du sport rendre le bien être accessible au plus grand nombre, partout dans le monde. Pour y parvenir, la data est au cœur de notre stratégie, elle guide chaque décision, de la conception du produit à l&#39;expérience client.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au cœur de l’entité Decathlon Digital, nous recherchons notre futur.e Senior Product Manager pour rejoindre les équipes Data Factory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cette plateforme technologique, globale à tout le groupe de manière internationale, soutient le développement de l’usage de la Data et de l’IA chez Decathlon, du calcul du chiffre d’affaires à l’aide de conception de produits innovants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous sommes garants des outils, de la scalabilité, de la mise en place et du respect des bonnes pratiques de développement. Nous accompagnons au quotidien l’ensemble des acteurs métiers tels que Data Analysts, Data Engineers, Analytics Engineers, Data Scientists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La Data Factory est conçue comme une&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Modern Data Stack&lt;/em&gt;, avec un lakehouse comme centre de gravité.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Elle est ensuite divisée en plusieurs équipes, chacune étant pilotée par un leader technique, avec comme ambition de travailler avec un.e Product Manager attitré.e.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre équipe&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Data Lake&lt;/strong&gt; est donc la brique fondamentale de cette mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre mission ? Mettre à disposition des solutions de stockage pour l’ensemble de la Data Platform de Decathlon, tout en garantissant la gouvernance, robustesse et scalabilité par défaut. Véritable pilier de la gouvernance technique du patrimoine de données, notre équipe gère les métadonnées via le metastore Unity Catalog et les data contracts, permettant ainsi de construire une observabilité globale de la plateforme (usage, lignage, etc.). Un terrain de jeu technique à fort impact et aux défis d&#39;envergure internationale !&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;L&#39;équipe est composée actuellement de :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 Product Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 Data Architect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 Data Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 Software Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 Ops Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exemples de&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;challenges actuels&lt;/strong&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Améliorer notre offre de support pour faciliter le parcours utilisateur (documentation, gestion des incidents, ...)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discussion avec les équipes Data/IA des pays et domaines sur leurs challenges du moment (données sensibles, données privées, ...) pour définir les priorités de nos équipes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comment faciliter la gouvernance des données ? Par exemple intégrer des règles automatiques de validation des données, data contractualization, ...&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rationalisation de notre offre et décommissionnement du legacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre ambition groupe, celle d’améliorer l’expérience digitale de nos clients, nous amène à une nouvelle approche orientée clients, une approche produit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le/La Product Manager de l&#39;équipe Data Lake:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquiert une compréhension de son périmètre, de l&#39;état de l’art sur le marché, du fonctionnement technique des outils associés.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Représente nos utilisateurs métiers, comprend leurs challenges et les retranscrit aux équipes techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accompagne la mise en œuvre de nouvelles fonctionnalités ou produits sur tout le cycle de vie (démo, formation, communication, documentation, …).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tu seras garant·e de l&#39;évolution et de la robustesse de ce produit critique pour l&#39;ensemble des équipes Decathlon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Tes missions principales s&#39;articuleront autour des axes suivants :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Vision &amp;amp; Delivery :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu pilotes le cycle complet du produit, de la Discovery à la coordination du Delivery en lien étroit avec le Leader. Tu traduis les enjeux business et techniques en une roadmap claire, priorisée et axée sur la valeur.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Projets Stratégiques :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu lead l&#39;End-of-Life (EOL) de notre Legacy, orchestres la migration vers la nouvelle infrastructure et designs les nouveaux espaces et fonctionnalités sur Unity Catalog.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Gouvernance &amp;amp; Excellence Opérationnelle :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu assures la gouvernance fine du metastore, la gestion des droits d&#39;accès et intègres au cœur de ta roadmap les enjeux de sécurité, de performance, de maintenance et de FinOps (optimisation des coûts cloud).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;9,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Leadership Fonctionnel &amp;amp; Synergies :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu assures le management fonctionnel de l&#39;équipe technique au quotidien et tu pourras être amené·e à animer un groupe transverse de PM sur des sujets communs afin de garantir l&#39;alignement de notre vision produit globale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Mesure de l&#39;impact :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu définis et suis les indicateurs clés de réussite focalisés sur la fiabilité, la robustesse de la plateforme et la mesure précise de l&#39;usage de tes produits. Tu co-animes le budget du produit avec le leader.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Expérience :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu justifies d&#39;au moins 5 ans d&#39;expérience comme Product Manager, avec une légitimité et une réussite reconnues sur des produits complexes ou de plateforme.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;11,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Expertise Technique &amp;amp; Data :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu possèdes une forte appétence technique ainsi qu&#39;une solide compréhension des enjeux liés à la gestion des données, aux accès et à la gouvernance. Savoir manipuler la donnée est un réel plus pour ce poste.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Culture Tech &amp;amp; IA :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu maîtrises les outils d&#39;Intelligence Artificielle appliqués au Product Management et tu appréhendes parfaitement les défis techniques sous-jacents (sécurité, infrastructure, scalabilité).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;11,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Soft Skills :&lt;/strong&gt; Orienté·e utilisateur, tu as un fort sens du service. Tu aimes écouter, creuser des sujets de fond et proposer des solutions innovantes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;11,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Fédérateur·rice :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu disposes d&#39;excellentes capacités de communication pour vulgariser des concepts complexes, dialoguer aussi bien avec des profils techniques que métiers, et fédérer autour de ta vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
